course: dictionary
lesson: 3380
title: Does it exist?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Exist means to be real, or to be present in the world or in a place. «Dinosaurs existed long ago» means they were real a very long time ago. Try it in the sentence: "Dinosaurs were real long ago" still makes sense.
explain: Exist can also mean to stay alive, especially in a hard way, like having to exist on very little food. Read the clues around the word to tell which meaning the writer wants.
explain: Exist has relatives. Existence is the noun, as in the existence of dinosaurs. Existed is the past tense, and existing means already there. «Rules exist so people don't crash into each other» means the rules are there for a reason.
explain: Being online does not prove that something exists. A bot can invent a book that does not exist, and it can sound very sure of itself. Always check whether a thing is real before you believe it.
fact: Exist means to be real or to be present in the world.
fact: «Existed» is the past tense of exist: «before that, the baby did not exist as a person.»
fact: Existence is the noun: it names the state of being real.
fact: When a bot invents an answer that is not true, people call it a hallucination.
fact: Extinct animals no longer exist.
exercise: «Dinosaurs existed long ago.» What does existed mean here? | *Were real, once living in the world | Were bright and shiny | Were lost in a shop | Were made of paper
exercise: «Rules like "walk, don't run" exist so people don't crash into each other in corridors.» Find and copy one word that means to be there and real. | rules | *exist | corridors | crash
exercise: A bot says a head teacher called Mrs Pike works here, but she is made up. What is the bot's made-up answer called? | A hologram | A hymn | *A hallucination | A hurricane
test: «Some animals no longer exist.» What does no longer exist mean? | They are very, very big | They are hidden in a cave | They have moved to a new house | *They are no longer real or alive
test: Which word is the noun for the state of being real? | existed | exists | *existence | existing
exam: «Clever fairness tricks exist: when two children share a cake, one cuts and the other chooses.» What does exist mean here? | Are eaten up quickly | Are made of cake | Are bought in a shop | *Are there and in use
